390
00:28:31,120 --> 00:28:50,714
Rym: Like if you separate the plot from the scenario, the plot is these are adventures and like irrespective of why they start and why they're poor, everybody's trying to go into this dungeon because this dungeon has some secret and it's a high fantasy world that is very similar to the kind of fantasy world that slayers is like.

391
00:28:51,075 --> 00:28:52,220
Rym: magic has rules.

392
00:28:52,500 --> 00:28:54,059
Scott: There's wizards, there's swords.

393
00:28:54,560 --> 00:28:54,632
Rym: Yup.

394
00:28:55,342 --> 00:28:57,840
Rym: There's knights, there's D&D based, you know.

395
00:28:58,100 --> 00:28:59,996
Rym: Like the standard types of fantasy races.

396
00:29:00,988 --> 00:29:01,600
Scott: There's orcs, dragons.

397
00:29:02,562 --> 00:29:05,600
Rym: And the plot itself is moderately compelling.

398
00:29:05,800 --> 00:29:06,959
Rym: The characters are pretty good.

399
00:29:07,541 --> 00:29:12,264
Rym: So yeah, the episodes are almost like 30%.

400
00:29:12,264 --> 00:29:13,577
Rym: There is a story here.

401
00:29:13,577 --> 00:29:16,199
Rym: 30% less than that.

402
00:29:16,880 --> 00:29:18,673
Rym: Well, there is a story here.

403
00:29:19,801 --> 00:29:21,919
Rym: I didn't say it was a particularly intense story.

404
00:29:22,460 --> 00:29:25,700
Scott: No, no, it's, but it's like, you know, there is a story, right?

405
00:29:25,761 --> 00:29:27,560
Scott: It's like we have a goal in this dungeon.

406
00:29:27,701 --> 00:29:29,680
Scott: There is a real thing going on, right?

407
00:29:30,081 --> 00:29:35,720
Scott: But it's like you're only mostly seeing them deal with the problem of getting food.

408
00:29:35,840 --> 00:29:50,320
Scott: It would be like if you had, uh, a TV show, like a real life TV show about, um, I don't know, a, uh, a car sales person.

409
00:29:50,340 --> 00:29:50,443
Scott: Right.

410
00:29:51,381 --> 00:29:59,579
Scott: And it's like, yeah, we let you know if car sales are going well, poorly, how their life is going a little bit, just so you understand who the person is.

411
00:30:00,130 --> 00:30:00,360
Scott: Right.

412
00:30:00,680 --> 00:30:07,880
Scott: But mostly we're going to be like, all the screen time is going to be going to the three meals a day that this person eats, right?

413
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:11,015
Scott: Because it's like, no matter what your job is, you got some food.

414
00:30:11,035 --> 00:30:11,820
Scott: you're eating, right?

415
00:30:11,920 --> 00:30:12,339
Scott: You're a human.

416
00:30:12,441 --> 00:30:13,480
Scott: You're not starving yourself.

417
00:30:13,604 --> 00:30:14,058
Scott: I hope not.

418
00:30:15,161 --> 00:30:26,159
Scott: So we're just going to show you, we're going to spend 20 out of the 30, 20, 25 out of the 30 minutes of screen time showing you this person cooking, eating, grocery shopping, et cetera.

419
00:30:26,740 --> 00:30:30,316
Scott: And the rest of the time, we're just sort of letting you know who they are and what's up in their life.

420
00:30:30,881 --> 00:30:34,280
Rym: Yeah, but it is like the plot is starting to evolve around them.

421
00:30:34,440 --> 00:30:40,900
Rym: Like a lot of the, on the way storytelling is building up to clearly this manga is going to deal with the dungeon itself.

422
00:30:41,081 --> 00:30:51,460
Rym: And clearly these adventures, again, I haven't read the manga, so I'm actually speculating from the 12 episodes of the show that have come out because that's literally the most, all I know about this show or this plot.

423
00:30:52,122 --> 00:31:02,172
Rym: But I feel like the fact that they're just eating in the dungeon and like entering the ecosystem of the dungeon means that the bigger plot is.

424
00:31:02,634 --> 00:31:04,878
Rym: that is actually the secret to the dungeon.

425
00:31:05,140 --> 00:31:10,560
Rym: They're going to get deeper than anyone's ever gotten because even though they're not the most powerful, they're, they're doing it.

426
00:31:10,760 --> 00:31:11,920
Scott: They're pretty powerful though, right?

427
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:20,800
Scott: It's like that usually a lot of these shows, the, the adventures are either going to be like really weak beginners and you see them level up over time right here.

428
00:31:20,981 --> 00:31:23,619
Scott: It's like they actually are pretty strong.

429
00:31:23,760 --> 00:31:28,780
Rym: They're like mid-level carry, like in D&D terms, they're like seventh or eighth level, like serious biz characters.

430
00:31:28,840 --> 00:31:30,780
Scott: I think they might be stronger than that even, right?

431
00:31:30,820 --> 00:31:37,920
Scott: They're obviously not like God tier or anything, but they're, you know, like mega wizards, but it's like, they're really powerful.

432
00:31:38,680 --> 00:31:46,600
Scott: They feel like what a level eight to 10 like characters, especially, you know, the highest level is actually the little thief guy who doesn't get enough screen time.

433
00:31:46,900 --> 00:31:47,200
Rym: Oh, chill Chuck.

434
00:31:47,700 --> 00:31:47,785
Scott: Yeah.

435
00:31:48,160 --> 00:31:50,020
Scott: He basically detects every trap.

436
00:31:50,200 --> 00:31:50,659
Scott: No problem.

437
00:31:50,921 --> 00:31:52,040
Scott: Never gets fooled by them.

438
00:31:52,140 --> 00:31:52,879
Rym: He's never wrong.

439
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:55,639
Rym: Whenever he says not to do something like they should have listened to him.

440
00:31:56,200 --> 00:31:56,300
Scott: Yeah.

441
00:31:56,360 --> 00:32:00,898
Scott: It's like he just seems less powerful because his skills are just thief skills and not kill monster skills.

442
00:32:01,260 --> 00:32:06,139
Rym: There's a great, there's a great moment where they're like, all right, we're going to do this and this and this and this to fight the thing.

443
00:32:06,463 --> 00:32:07,840
Rym: And then he, and they're like, what are you going to do?

444
00:32:07,900 --> 00:32:08,740
Rym: He's like, the fuck?

445
00:32:08,781 --> 00:32:09,480
Rym: I'm not doing anything.

446
00:32:09,500 --> 00:32:10,560
Rym: I'm a thief, but I'm not here.

447
00:32:10,761 --> 00:32:11,937
Rym: That's not the part I'm good at.

448
00:32:12,360 --> 00:32:14,140
Scott: My goal was an episode that highlighted him.

449
00:32:14,281 --> 00:32:15,259
Scott: Episode three maybe.

450
00:32:15,421 --> 00:32:17,180
Rym: But it was like, my job is to get you there.

451
00:32:17,260 --> 00:32:19,359
Rym: My job is not to directly fight the dragon dudes.

452
00:32:19,800 --> 00:32:20,818
Rym: Like you keep forgetting this.

453
00:32:22,982 --> 00:32:25,240
Rym: But the characters are really endearing along the way.

454
00:32:25,320 --> 00:32:33,960
Rym: But what I really want to focus on is that the structure of the episodes is just, it's leaning into the cooking show aspect in a very apt way.

455
00:32:34,020 --> 00:32:36,980
Rym: Cause one studio trigger, they understood the mission.

456
00:32:37,560 --> 00:32:46,300
Rym: You have to make the cooking part of the show be ghibli levels of, I want to eat that as the viewer, even though it's monsters.

457
00:32:47,061 --> 00:32:53,879
Rym: And right away, I said every episode I'd like, if we haven't eaten dinner, I really want to eat what they're cooking.

458
00:32:54,062 --> 00:32:55,479
Rym: Like up to the point that I'll draw it.

459
00:32:55,680 --> 00:32:59,220
Rym: It's, it's just ghibli level animation of the cooking process.

460
00:32:59,481 --> 00:33:07,579
Scott: Well, and then when the meal is, when the meal is done, they always have this like still frame that they sort of slowly zoom out of like straight out of a Japanese travel show.

461
00:33:08,290 --> 00:33:08,520
Scott: Yeah.

462
00:33:08,620 --> 00:33:15,659
Scott: And it's like the best drawing they can make of the food and like a big text that says what the food is.

463
00:33:15,820 --> 00:33:22,419
Scott: And then like the sound effect, like doo doo, like ta da, the food, here it is, the meal.

464
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:23,146
Rym: Yup.

465
00:33:23,760 --> 00:33:45,660
Rym: But what's really clever is that the cooking, this is going to sound weird to say the process of the cooking is extremely realistic, despite the fact that none of the ingredients are real, because they, they basically describe a process of preparing food that is along the lines of what a similar real world dish would be.

466
00:33:45,860 --> 00:33:53,200
Rym: Like this kind of meat with these kinds of risks has to be done this way or the bit where like he takes a bite of the thing before they cook it.

467
00:33:53,260 --> 00:33:55,519
Rym: And then later it gets food poisoning when he bit it.

468
00:33:55,842 --> 00:33:58,540
Rym: We're sitting there and Emily's like, why doesn't he get food poisoning?

469
00:33:58,701 --> 00:34:01,259
Rym: And then five minutes later in the show, we're like, well.

470
00:34:05,361 --> 00:34:16,420
Scott: Yeah, you know, there's a lot of sci-fis and fantasies that do that, where they take the rules of the real world, apply them to something fantastical while keeping a lot of the truths intact.

471
00:34:16,900 --> 00:34:19,880
Scott: It's like, this is true about eating lamb meat.

472
00:34:20,300 --> 00:34:23,659
Scott: We'll just teach, we'll just, which is a real thing in the real world.

473
00:34:24,061 --> 00:34:28,199
Scott: So we'll take that and we'll just say that it's also true for cooking monster meat.

474
00:34:29,324 --> 00:34:34,679
Rym: They pulled me in too, because they're early on, there's the episode where it's like, where it says she's like, I want to eat the living armor.

475
00:34:34,821 --> 00:34:36,679
Rym: And everyone's like, that's literally impossible.

476
00:34:36,802 --> 00:34:37,558
Rym: What's wrong with you?

477
00:34:38,002 --> 00:34:41,100
Rym: And even I, the viewer was like, okay, they're not going to eat the living armor.

478
00:34:41,239 --> 00:34:42,940
Rym: Clearly they'll eat something else in this episode.

479
00:34:43,440 --> 00:34:47,280
Rym: And then by the end of the episode, when they eat the living armor, it was just fantastic.

480
00:34:49,443 --> 00:34:51,120
Rym: Like that was an A plus moment.

481
00:34:51,840 --> 00:34:58,760
Scott: But then, you know, there's always, you could sort of actually see through that one because it's like, you know, they're going to eat it somehow, even though it's made of metal.

482
00:34:59,000 --> 00:34:59,996
Scott: I wonder what it could be.

483
00:35:00,561 --> 00:35:07,079
Rym: I thought Senshi was going to eat it because he's a dwarf and he just could, but they went way better than what I thought was going to happen.

484
00:35:08,561 --> 00:35:19,695
Rym: But then you get a kind of a good turnabout and the tone shift, the same way that slayers would have the tone shift at a certain point where toward the end of what we've seen so far.

485
00:35:20,042 --> 00:35:20,833
Scott: I've only seen four.

486
00:35:21,861 --> 00:35:22,580
Rym: Oh, oh, okay.

487
00:35:22,840 --> 00:35:24,059
Scott: So I watched the orc episode.

488
00:35:24,381 --> 00:35:36,700
Rym: Let's say they get to a point where they discover a dead body that is, uh, extremely realistic, gruesome, like problem body and food on it.

489
00:35:36,980 --> 00:35:46,280
Rym: And they're gonna, they're gonna do a resurrection thing and they animate and step through the process of like, we got to sort the bones.

490
00:35:46,562 --> 00:35:47,479
Rym: We got to do this.

491
00:35:47,782 --> 00:35:49,540
Rym: Is that a human bone or a war bone?

492
00:35:49,941 --> 00:35:53,000
Rym: Like get the blood off the, get the skin off the skull.

493
00:35:53,140 --> 00:36:07,200
Rym: Like they do all the steps, just like the cooking show, except it's 100% dead serious and more like a medical drama to do the resurrection spell and applying the process of cooking to everything you do, even if it's not cooking.

494
00:36:07,380 --> 00:36:07,540
Scott: Yup.

495
00:36:07,940 --> 00:36:09,920
Rym: They pull it off perfectly.

496
00:36:10,182 --> 00:36:12,158
Rym: It is such a fantastic scene.

497
00:36:12,900 --> 00:36:17,900
Scott: It's like if you play shock social science fiction and your only conflict resolution mechanisms are stabbing and cooking.

498
00:36:18,181 --> 00:36:20,380
Scott: So sometimes I want to resurrect someone.

499
00:36:20,480 --> 00:36:21,960
Scott: Well, I'm not going to resurrect them by stabbing.

500
00:36:22,080 --> 00:36:30,857
Rym: I guess I'll resurrect them by cooking for, for the listeners unaware because you wouldn't know about the, the, the role playing system by Mr.

501
00:36:31,980 --> 00:36:36,340
Rym: Newman shock social science fiction, which I think got a second edition that we never played or even read.

502
00:36:36,781 --> 00:36:44,900
Rym: But, uh, this is literally a role playing system where you play in a world like a dnd world or a space world or whatever.

503
00:36:45,240 --> 00:36:48,320
Rym: But literally science, it doesn't make sense.

504
00:36:48,561 --> 00:36:55,502
Rym: Like, unless it's deep science fiction, that's addressing social issues, but literally the rules are.

505
00:36:56,184 --> 00:37:02,000
Rym: there are two ways to resolve all conflicts at the table, no exceptions.

506
00:37:02,500 --> 00:37:06,520
Rym: So as a group, you decide what those two options are and that's it.

507
00:37:07,101 --> 00:37:09,780
Rym: Everything is literally framed that way in the game.

508
00:37:09,841 --> 00:37:10,620
Rym: And it's fantastic.

509
00:37:10,962 --> 00:37:13,560
Rym: And it is so applicable to how delicious and dungeon proceeds.

510
00:37:13,760 --> 00:37:14,196
Rym: It's perfect.

511
00:37:16,602 --> 00:37:22,260
Scott: So, uh, so yeah, the one thing I got to say is that, you know, it's studio trigger comes in and so you're expecting, right?

512
00:37:22,360 --> 00:37:31,398
Scott: These are the people who brought you inferno cop, kill la kill, kill la kill, uh, uh, little witch academia from air.

513
00:37:32,509 --> 00:37:32,717
Scott: Yup.

514
00:37:33,120 --> 00:37:41,860
Scott: So you're expecting it to be bombastic off the wall, extreme, like so anime, right?

515
00:37:44,383 --> 00:37:48,340
Scott: Um, and it really isn't because they're got this manga that they're adapting, right?

516
00:37:48,400 --> 00:37:55,318
Scott: A lot of those other ones were, you know, originals, um, and whatnot that was like mostly them or all them.

517
00:37:55,862 --> 00:37:58,540
Scott: And so they could put their, their sort of own style on it.

518
00:37:58,620 --> 00:38:02,320
Scott: But when you're sort of adapting a manga, you have to stick to the manga.

519
00:38:03,341 --> 00:38:12,320
Scott: Uh, but you can see there are certain scenes where they are able to find like a time and place where they can make some studio triggerness.

520
00:38:12,540 --> 00:38:19,480
Scott: And the one that stood out to me the most was I think episode maybe two where there was like a flashback to the past for the elf or something.

521
00:38:19,740 --> 00:38:21,640
Rym: Oh yeah, I know what you're talking about.

522
00:38:22,060 --> 00:38:22,160
Rym: Yeah.

523
00:38:22,360 --> 00:38:34,819
Scott: And you could, I was like, Oh, here they, here they finally found a spot where they could be studio trigger and still be themselves and not just be an anime studio for hire, you know, adapting a manga, you know, rotely.

524
00:38:35,101 --> 00:38:41,520
Rym: I just imagine in the studio, like, look, I know you want to animate planets exploding on a galactic scale.

525
00:38:41,860 --> 00:38:47,920
Rym: I want you to take all that energy and animate this piece of steak, but with that level of intensity, that's your mission.

526
00:38:48,180 --> 00:38:50,777
Scott: I think we might see some of that when, you know, there's more dragons.

527
00:38:51,720 --> 00:38:57,900
Rym: Well, spoilers for episodes 11 and 12, they fight a dragon and you get some dragon fighting animation.

528
00:38:58,620 --> 00:38:59,014
Scott: There you go.

529
00:39:00,401 --> 00:39:01,879
Rym: But it's not the best show.

530
00:39:02,140 --> 00:39:03,120
Rym: Like this show is good.

531
00:39:03,361 --> 00:39:10,020
Rym: This is the kind of show, like when we were at RIT anime, obviously we would show all four episodes of this, like as soon as possible.

532
00:39:10,400 --> 00:39:14,659
Rym: And people would be yelling and screaming in the audience, but this is not like an S tier anime.

533
00:39:14,780 --> 00:39:19,060
Rym: It's just a good anime that I would recommend watching if you're hankering for some anime.

534
00:39:19,807 --> 00:39:19,895
Scott: Yeah.

535
00:39:20,080 --> 00:39:30,240
Scott: It's like a lot of those scenario based shows, the premises, premises, they sound fun, but you actually watch those shows and they're sort of quite low brow.

536
00:39:31,003 --> 00:39:32,019
Rym: They're rarely good.

537
00:39:32,181 --> 00:39:34,780
Rym: Like skip them unless someone you trust says they're good.

538
00:39:35,442 --> 00:39:38,359
Scott: They're usually just sort of trashy, right?

539
00:39:39,180 --> 00:39:48,240
Scott: Whereas here it's like, Hey, you know, this is actually something that is solid, entertaining, has a story to follow.

540
00:39:48,380 --> 00:39:50,039
Scott: Is it have anything big to say?

541
00:39:50,740 --> 00:39:59,139
Scott: No, well, but it has a little bit more to say about, you know, food, where food comes from, et cetera, has a little bit to say.

542
00:39:59,760 --> 00:40:04,400
Rym: It gets a little more as it progresses into the concept of ecosystems and sustainability.

543
00:40:04,721 --> 00:40:08,659
Rym: Like it starts addressing that pretty directly and it keeps bringing it up.

544
00:40:09,481 --> 00:40:11,712
Rym: And clearly that's, that's the ultimate meta plot.

545
00:40:11,792 --> 00:40:13,500
Rym: is that the whole thing, right?

546
00:40:13,580 --> 00:40:16,820
Scott: So it has a little bit to say, but nothing enormous to say.

547
00:40:18,201 --> 00:40:23,660
Scott: But you know, and it's just enjoyable and not a waste of your time, right?

548
00:40:23,700 --> 00:40:37,720
Scott: Whereas I think if I actually wanted to watch someone leveled up on a thousand slimes to become the most powerful that I probably only needed to watch the first episode and the last episode on two X speed to get everything I need out of it.

549
00:40:38,821 --> 00:40:47,960
Rym: But one thing I think is not worth, we should at least mention is that the show has drama and like has action and all that and the cooking, but it is legitimately funny.

550
00:40:48,500 --> 00:40:50,080
Rym: The characters are pretty good characters.

551
00:40:50,140 --> 00:40:57,999
Rym: The only weird thing about it to me is that the elf character acts a lot more the way I would think a human would act.

552
00:40:58,600 --> 00:41:07,420
Rym: And meanwhile, the human characters act a lot more like how I would expect a non-human character to act like the elf is not how you imagine elves.

553
00:41:07,800 --> 00:41:10,720
Rym: Elves might just be weirder in this universe.

554
00:41:10,821 --> 00:41:11,759
Rym: They're not talking elves.

555
00:41:11,841 --> 00:41:12,758
Rym: They're a different kind of elf.

556
00:41:13,840 --> 00:41:25,317
Scott: The elf is, I mean, the defining characteristic of the elf is that she's the one who's weirded out by all the foods and doesn't want to eat them, but then eventually eats them and they're delicious and yet doesn't learn her lesson ever.

557
00:41:27,061 --> 00:41:35,140
Scott: And even when the food is normal, like, like she's drooling and happy because they're going to eat normal foods like carrots or lettuces and cabbages.

558
00:41:35,391 --> 00:41:35,559
Scott: Right.

559
00:41:36,084 --> 00:41:37,036
Scott: And she's like, and breads.

560
00:41:37,502 --> 00:41:39,020
Scott: And she's like, Hooray, normal food.

561
00:41:39,142 --> 00:41:39,739
Scott: I want to eat it.

562
00:41:39,820 --> 00:41:40,360
Scott: I want to eat it.

563
00:41:40,360 --> 00:41:42,579
Scott: And you're like, finally, you're not complaining about the food.

564
00:41:43,121 --> 00:41:46,620
Scott: And then she's like, Oh, but this food was grown in poop.

565
00:41:46,881 --> 00:41:50,700
Scott: And it's like food on the surface is growing in poop, too.

566
00:41:51,420 --> 00:41:56,919
Scott: This is why are you just grossed out by literally any food you would ever eat?

567
00:41:57,620 --> 00:41:59,160
Scott: It's like only lamb bread.

568
00:41:59,484 --> 00:42:00,638
Scott: Good enough for you and nothing else.

569
00:42:02,622 --> 00:42:03,707
Scott: I don't know what's up with this.

570
00:42:03,828 --> 00:42:06,320
Scott: elf is like, literally, it's like, stop it already.

571
00:42:06,380 --> 00:42:08,859
Scott: You've been grossed out by the food before eating it.

572
00:42:09,383 --> 00:42:10,840
Scott: Four or five episodes in a row.

573
00:42:10,961 --> 00:42:12,519
Scott: However many I imagine all of them.

574
00:42:13,023 --> 00:42:14,879
Scott: And then you eat it and it's delicious every time.

575
00:42:15,464 --> 00:42:17,219
Scott: Oh, I don't know next time.

576
00:42:17,841 --> 00:42:23,439
Rym: I don't know if it was mentioned in the show or not because I didn't know this, but apparently she's a half elf, which might explain a lot.

577
00:42:24,065 --> 00:42:24,340
Scott: Okay.

578
00:42:24,789 --> 00:42:24,998
Scott: All right.

579
00:42:25,280 --> 00:42:25,676
Scott: Didn't know that.

580
00:42:25,960 --> 00:42:26,056
Rym: Yeah.

581
00:42:26,200 --> 00:42:26,697
Rym: Didn't know that.

582
00:42:27,024 --> 00:42:27,680
Rym: If that's a spoiler.

583
00:42:27,904 --> 00:42:28,200
Rym: Sorry.

584
00:42:28,300 --> 00:42:29,420
Rym: That's like the top of Wikipedia.

585
00:42:29,540 --> 00:42:30,052
Rym: So what do you want?

586
00:42:30,781 --> 00:42:31,014
Scott: Okay.

587
